# Engine caches and local editor state
.godot/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Video/audio RENDERS and generated distribution packages stay outside source
# control. The game's own music is not one of those and is tracked: Assests/
# lives outside this repository, so godot/audio/magic_cliffs.ogg is the only
# copy a clone gets, exactly as for every generated sheet under godot/. Note
# .ogg is deliberately absent from the list below.
#
# godot/audio/ is unignored below for the same reason, one format later. The
# opening's voice-over is an mp3 and it is a game asset, not a render: without
# the exception a clone gets ui/storyboard.gd loading a file that is not there,
# and the first thing a new player sees is a silent one.
*.[mM][pP]3
!godot/audio/*.mp3
*.[mM][pP]4
*.avi
*.mov
# Same exception again, and for a sharper reason than the mp3 one. The boss
# track is decisive_battle.wav and it was ignored by this line with no
# exception under it, so only its .import was ever committed: every clone
# reached BOTH dragon fights with no battle music at all, and the tests did
# not catch it because they compared a track NAME rather than a stream. It is
# 20 MB, which is the price of there being no Vorbis encoder here — encode it
# (see godot/audio/PROVENANCE.md) and the .ogg supersedes it, because music.gd
# looks for .ogg first and .ogg is deliberately not listed above.
*.wav
!godot/audio/*.wav
exports/
builds/

# Local credentials/configuration
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
credentials/
*.p12
*.pfx

# Git cannot ignore by size: inspect staged files before committing (>25 MB).

# Generated evidence, all of it. Every capture folder here is reproducible in
# one command from godot/tests/capture_*.gd, and every timestamped report is
# written afresh by the test suites, so none of it belongs in the repository —
# it accumulated to 90 reports and 79 PNGs before this rule existed.
#
# build-manifest.json and screens/ used to be excepted, because the manifest is
# the deliverable and screens/ is linked from README.md. The rule is now the
# whole folder, with exactly one exception: evidence/screens/title-01-new-journey.png
# is tracked, force-added past this rule with `git add -f`, because it is the
# README's title image and GitHub renders only what the repository carries. A
# file already tracked is not re-ignored, so it stays tracked without an
# unignore rule — do not "tidy" it out. Everything else here is regenerated
# before a release rather than committed, including the manifest, whose hashes
# name files no fresh clone carries.
evidence/
